==============================================================================
ARM 2 -- THE TEST: hold the master at PERFECT, move only the SOURCES
==============================================================================
The master is `lat` in every row: a literally perfect reconstruction,
identical pixels, unchanged. ONLY the source blur changes. If 3.4867
is a ceiling on perfection, every row must read 3.4867.

  sources (box half-width)    RECONSTRUCT    vs 3.4867
  ----------------------------------------------------
  (1, 2, 3, 4)                     1.0000        0.29x
  (2, 3, 4, 5)                     3.4867        1.00x
  (3, 4, 5, 6)                     4.2479        1.22x
  (4, 5, 6, 7)                     5.1014        1.46x
  (5, 6, 7, 8)                     6.3216        1.81x
  (6, 7, 8, 9)                     8.3201        2.39x
  (8, 9, 10, 11)                  20.2615        5.81x
  (10, 11, 12, 13)                18.3969        5.28x

  RECONSTRUCT ranges 1.0000 .. 20.2615 over an UNCHANGED, perfect master.
  spread 20.26x

  VERDICT: 3.4867 is NOT A CEILING. The master is byte-identical in
  every row above -- it is the same perfect reconstruction -- and the
  number moves by 20.26x purely because the SOURCES changed. The arm
  measures how blurred the best source is, not how good the master is.
  A real subject scoring above 3.4867 is therefore NOT out-performing
  perfection; it has source frames blurred by more than a k=2 box.

